<h2>Top Stories</h2><br/>
<h3>Apple Adds Facial Unlock Option on iPhone Duo in iOS 27.3</h3><br/>
One of the biggest complaints about Apple's new foldable iPhone Duo is that authentication takes place via a Touch ID power button rather than through Face ID, but that's changing a bit in the upcoming iOS 27.3 update.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/11/iphone-duo-yellow-hand.jpeg" alt="" width="2500" height="1406" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1076171" /><br/>
Apple is <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/16/iphone-duo-face-unlock/">launching a new face unlock option</a> that will unlock your phone using the front camera, but given it's less secure than true Face ID, there are some significant limits. It requires a recent Touch ID or passcode authorization to have happened within the previous 45 minutes, and it can only be used to unlock the phone, not to authorize Apple Pay purchases, autofill passwords, or take other higher-security actions.<br/>
<br/>
The latest iOS 27.3 beta also sees the <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/16/apple-icloud-paid-siri-ai-upgrade/">rollout of daily Siri AI limits</a> and details on how much additional usage you get with various tiers of iCloud+ plans, so be sure to check out our <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/16/ios-27-3-beta-2-everything-new/">overview of everything new in iOS 27.3 beta 2</a>, as well as our <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/16/iphone-duo-face-unlock-hands-on/">hands-on video that shows off the new face unlock feature</a>.<br/>
<br/>
The unlock feature is in some ways a stopgap, as <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/15/apple-aims-to-upgrade-iphone-duo-in-four-ways/">true Face ID is one of Apple's highest priorities for the second-generation model</a>, alongside several other improvements.<br/>
<br/>
