<h3>Apple Blames Internal Update for Outage, Says It Wasn't a Cyberattack</h3><br/>
Apple experienced a <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/17/apple-accounts-experiencing-issues/">significant outage of some of its platforms</a> on Tuesday of this week, with various services reliant upon Apple Account and iCloud sign-ins going down. Apple retail stores also experienced difficulties processing transactions.<br/>
<br/>
<img src="https://images.macrumors.com/article-new/2026/01/Apple-Logo-Black.jpeg" alt="" width="2048" height="1145" class="aligncenter size-full wp-image-1034439" /><br/>
Apple says the issue was the result of an <a href="https://www.macrumors.com/2026/11/17/apple-accounts-experiencing-issues/">unspecified "internal update" and not due to a cyberattack</a>.<br/>
